<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Marathon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">490 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-persian-wars">Greco-Persian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Marathon was fought in 490 BCE on the plain of Marathon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a>, where an Athenian army, aided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-plataea">Plataea</a>, defeated a Persian expeditionary force sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a>. It ended the first Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-persian-invasion-of-greece">invasion of Greece</a>. For the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> the setback was limited in scale, but the battle became a central symbol of Greek resistance to Persian expansion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-marathon.jpg" alt="Battle of Marathon" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Steeple Davis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scene_of_the_Battle_of_Marathon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
